  "releaseNotes": "Added\n- ActivityDiagnosticsMode property in SmppClientBase for enabling or disabling Inetlab.SMPP Activity diagnostics per SMPP client. Disabled by default.\n\nFixed\n- Dispose Activity instances for throttled SMPP requests to prevent memory retention in telemetry scenarios.\n- Prevent ambient Activity capture by the long-lived connection transfer loop.\n- Use ActivityContext with TTL-based cleanup for DLR trace correlation, so related DeliverSm can continue the same TraceId without unbounded MessageId correlation growth.\n- Prevent `SendSpeedLimit` from accumulating scheduler delay between queued sends, which could slow throttled traffic and make send timing less stable.",
  "requireLicenseAcceptance": true,
